notes:
Firewall - Filters traffic.
  Firewall categories:
    Stateful - Rather than inspecting an individual packet, this firewall determines the behaviour of a device based uupon the entire connection.
    Stateless - Uses a stitic set of rules to determine whether or not individual packets are acceptable or not.
VPN (Virtual private network) - Allows devices to separate networks to communicate securely by createing a dedicated path between each other over the internet (tunnel).
  Benefits of VPN - Allows to networks in different geographical locations to be connected, offers privacy and anonymity.
    Technology:
      PPP - Allows authentication and provides encryption of data. VPNs work by using a private key and public certificate. (Not capable of leaving a network by itself (non-routable))
      PPTP (Point to point tunneling protocol) - Allows data from PPP to travel and leave a network. Weakly encrypted to alternatives. Easy to set up and supported by most devices.
      IPSec (Internet protocol security) - Encrypts data using the existing IP framework. Difficult to setup. Strong encryption. Supported by many devices.
VLAN (Virtual local area network) - Allows specific devices within a network to be virtually split up. For example sales department (VLAN 1) and accounting department (VLAN 2).

